      "claim": "Results are reported stratified by parent heavy-atom count.",
      "reason": "The parent allocator correction measured that drawn parents are median 9-15 heavy atoms with 30-40 percent under 10, several of them degenerate 1-3 atom fragments. A chemistry prior cannot make a good drug out of a one-atom parent in one edit, so an unstratified aggregate cannot separate 'the prior does not work' from 'the parents are fragments'. Both readings are reported."
